<keyword_extraction_rules>
  <purpose>
    keyword_tokens are used for exact substring matching against document titles and content.
    All tokens apply AND logic — every token must appear in a document for it to be returned.
    More tokens narrow results; generic tokens destroy recall.
  </purpose>

  <rules>
    <rule id="0" name="preserve_ambiguous_terms">
      Acronyms, abbreviations, or terms with multiple plausible meanings must never be
      translated, expanded, or resolved. Add them in their original form only if they meet
      the Tier 1-2 specificity threshold. Generic words are still excluded even if ambiguous.
      <good>"UT" → keyword_tokens: ["UT"]</good>
      <bad>"UT" → keyword_tokens: ["unit test"] (abbreviation was resolved)</bad>
      <good>"결과" → excluded (generic word, Rule 2 applies regardless)</good>
    </rule>

    <rule id="1" name="known_sources_only">
      A keyword must come from exactly one of these two sources, verbatim:
      - The user's original question (specific terms the user actually wrote)
      - Previously retrieved documents (exact identifiers or terms seen in ToolMessage results)

      Do NOT invent keywords to describe search intent.
      Do NOT add typo-corrected or inferred forms — only the exact string from the source.
      Corrected or expanded terms belong in query only, where vector search absorbs the uncertainty.
    </rule>

    <rule id="2" name="no_generic_words">
      Skip a term if it is too common to be distinctive, even if it comes from a known source.
      <bad>token, API, schema, performance, error, migration, data, system</bad>
      <good>ChatTokenUsage, token_breakdown, jsonb_object_agg, CATDEV-310, cutover, 집계 버그</good>
    </rule>

    <rule id="3" name="no_forced_translation">
      Use the exact form as it appears in the source. Never translate between Korean and English.
    </rule>

    <rule id="4" name="specificity_tiers">
      Select 0-3 tokens, prioritized by tier. When in doubt, leave empty.
      <tier level="1" label="unique_identifiers">
        Ticket IDs, class/function/column names
        (e.g., CATDEV-123, ChatTokenUsage, token_breakdown)
      </tier>
      <tier level="2" label="specific_proper_nouns">
        Library, module, or exact feature names
        (e.g., pgvector, Langfuse, HNSW)
      </tier>
      <tier level="3" label="distinctive_domain_terms">
        Distinctive domain terms in their original language
        (e.g., cutover, reducer, 집계 버그)
      </tier>
      Default to empty. Only populate when you have at least one Tier 1 or Tier 2 term.
      A search with no keywords is better than a search with generic keywords.
    </rule>
  </rules>
</keyword_extraction_rules>
